WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.680
For almost 10 years, Dos Equis has been engaging
beer consumers with its "Most Interesting

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.750
Man in the World" campaign, featuring an elegant
older man recalling mind-blowing life adventures

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.230
from the good ol' days.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:16.940
Those videos have made 77-year-old American
actor Jonathan Goldsmith a pop culture celebrity.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.320
But in an effort to attract a younger audience,
Dos Equis recently passed the prestigious

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.509
mantle to a younger actor, Augustin Legrand.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.520
“Think anyone will ever be as interesting
as him?”

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.300
Here are a few things you don't know about
the new most interesting man in the world.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.300
More modern

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:43.170
At 41 at the time of his hiring, Legrand is
more than 30 years younger than Goldsmith.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.219
The new commercials highlight the contrast
right away: the previous versions basked in

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:51.010
past glories while vintage video footage of
his adventures plays.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.410
But Legrand seems to show a more present man
of mystery.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:55.859
Dos Equis told Ad Week,

00:00:55.859 --> 00:01:00.329
"The new Most Interesting Man is a man of
our times, and in this first glimpse, he shares

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:05.269
hints of being a resourceful, rough and tumble
guy, who remains a jack-of-all-trades hero

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:08.900
that one would expect from the man bearing
this infamous title."

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.750
That, and this guy was busy.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.170
“Bringo!”

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.630
A master of many tongues

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:21.640
Legrand is a French actor who boasts a trilingual
skillset, speaking English, French, and Spanish.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:26.049
It's interesting to note that in his Dos Equis
debut, Legrand's first line is actually in

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:26.589
Spanish.

00:01:26.589 --> 00:01:28.091
"It's hard to say."

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.670
The beer brand tells USA Today there's a reason
for that, saying,

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:33.750
"We're trying to reach a new audience.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.329
The reality of the drinker base is it's much
more multicultural than ever.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:40.300
And Spanish-dominant consumers are increasingly
important."

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.409
Muy bien, as they say.

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:44.399
Nearly the most boring man

00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:48.659
Before he became the new Most Interesting
Man, Legrand almost became a total snooze

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:51.200
when he earned a Master's degree in tax law.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.700
But by a weird turn of fate, Legrand was bitten
by the acting bug and enrolled at French drama

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.899
school Cours Florent in Paris.

00:01:58.899 --> 00:02:03.490
He's since been featured on the big and small
screen since 2001, including a recurring role

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.939
in the French TV drama Odysseus, and the 2006
film Flyboys.

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:09.459
Actor and activist

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:14.209
As proof of his impressive moral character,
Legrand is also the co-founder of the Children

00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:18.900
of Don Quixote, an organization dedicated
to raising awareness of France's homeless

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:19.900
population.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:25.050
Beginning in 2006, the organization helped
to install 100 tents on a canal near the Seine,

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:28.840
and has repeated the installation multiple
times over the years.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.370
Legrand's documentary on the topic received
an Amnesty Award nomination at the Copenhagen

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.400
International Documentary Festival.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.650
He's also opened an inexpensive organic restaurant
in Paris, so his real life might be even more

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.489
interesting than the role he plays on TV.

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:45.519
New man, same narrator

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:49.151
While there's a new Most Interesting Man,
the company still plans on introducing the

00:02:49.151 --> 00:02:51.700
video commercials with the same narrator,
Will Lyman.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.840
"His beard alone has experienced more than
a lesser man’s entire body."

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.760
Lyman was chosen to keep the familiar voice
going forward in Legrand's era, according

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.959
to brand manager Andre Woldt, who said,

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:05.091
"We feel he is an important part of the campaign.

00:03:05.091 --> 00:03:09.519
And while we want to evolve what interesting
means today, I think a few [tenets] of the

00:03:09.519 --> 00:03:11.010
brand are very important to keep."

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:14.770
...and that apparently means keeping the same
guy who narrates The History Channel's most

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:15.920
questionable content.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:23.019
"Deep sea UFOs continue to lurk through the
uncharted waters of Earth."

00:03:23.019 --> 00:03:24.019
Thanks for watching!

